names></name><name><surname>Deka</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferrell</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Shriver</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Estimating African American admixture proportions by use of population-specific alleles</article-title><source>Am J Hum Genet</source><year>1998</year><volume>63</volume><fpage>1839</fpage><lpage>1851</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9837836</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/302148</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Salas</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Richards</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lareu</surname><given-names>MV</given-names></name><name><surname>Scozzari</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Coppa</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Torroni</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Macaulay</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Carracedo</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The African diaspora: mitochondrial DNA and the Atlantic slave trade</article-title><source>Am J Hum Genet</source><year>2004</year><volume>74</volume><fpage>454</fpage><lpage>465</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14872407</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/382194</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Weale</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Gratrix</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Fletcher</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></nam